---
import CaseLayout from '../layouts/CaseLayout.astro';
---
<CaseLayout
  title="Ajna Design System · Deepali Pathe"
  caseNum="03"
  caseName="Ajna Design System"
>
  <main class="page">
    <div class="wrap">

      <!-- Hero -->
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          <span class="num">03</span><span>·</span><span>Design System · Internal Tools · 2025</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="page-title"><span class="accent">Ajna</span> <em>Design System.</em></h1>
        <p class="page-lede">
          Bringing structure, speed, and dark mode to internal tools, so every team stops <em>reinventing the same button.</em>
        </p>
        <div class="role-badges">
          <span class="role-badge">Design Systems</span>
          <span class="role-badge">Figma Variables</span>
          <span class="role-badge">Dark Mode</span>
          <span class="role-badge">Component Architecture</span>
          <span class="role-badge">Developer Handoff</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="page-meta reveal">
        <div class="row"><span class="k">Project</span><span class="v">Ajna Design System</span></div>
        <div class="row"><span class="k">Role</span><span class="v">Product Designer</span></div>
        <div class="row"><span class="k">Type</span><span class="v">Internal tools · System</span></div>
        <div class="row"><span class="k">Year</span><span class="v">2025</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="cover reveal">
        <img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dfim5nugc/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/thumb-designsystem_me3aqc" alt="Ajna Design System" />
      </div>

      <!-- 01 Problem -->
      <section class="section reveal">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="num">01</span><span>The problem</span></div>
        <h2 class="section-h">
          Every team was designing <em>the same button.</em>
          <span class="quiet">Again. And again. And again.</span>
        </h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Internal tools lacked visual consistency. Buttons, forms, layouts — every team was building them from scratch, wasting time and introducing inconsistencies that compounded across products. Developers spent hours in back-and-forth over specs that should have been self-evident. Designers wanted templates they could trust.</p>
        </div>
        <h3 class="sub-h">Research insights</h3>
        <div class="insight-list">
          <div class="insight-card"><span class="n">01</span><p>Inconsistent visual patterns across tools.</p></div>
          <div class="insight-card"><span class="n">02</span><p>Developers needed cleaner specs to reduce back-and-forth.</p></div>
          <div class="insight-card"><span class="n">03</span><p>Designers wanted ready-made templates and variants to move faster.</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="built-for">Built for: Product &amp; engineering teams · Designers · Developers</p>
      </section>

      <!-- 02 Role -->
      <section class="section reveal">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="num">02</span><span>My role</span></div>
        <h2 class="section-h">Not just designing components. <span class="accent">Architecting decisions.</span></h2>
        <ol class="num-list">
          <li><span class="n">01</span><span>Structured components using variants and variables.</span></li>
          <li><span class="n">02</span><span>Applied Figma variable modes to enable one-click dark mode.</span></li>
          <li><span class="n">03</span><span>Used auto layout + variables to ensure responsive behavior.</span></li>
          <li><span class="n">04</span><span>Documented usage and worked closely with developers to ensure feasibility.</span></li>
          <li><span class="n">05</span><span>Explored edge cases through real-world use and feedback loops.</span></li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <!-- 03 The System -->
      <section class="section reveal">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="num">03</span><span>The system</span></div>
        <h2 class="section-h">Tokens, <em>not opinions.</em></h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Every visual decision — color, spacing, type, borders — was encoded into tokens that scale across contexts and switch themes in one click.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="token-grid">
          <div class="token-card">
            <div class="token-card-head"><h4>Buttons &amp; Links</h4><span class="count">8 variants</span></div>
            <p>Primary, Secondary (1 &amp; 2), Tertiary (1 &amp; 2), Error, Success, Warning, Informational — each with Default, Hover, Active, Focus and Disabled states.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="token-card">
            <div class="token-card-head"><h4>Text &amp; Icons</h4><span class="count">8 semantic colors</span></div>
            <p>Primary, Secondary (1 &amp; 2), Tertiary, Error, Success, Warning, Informational — mapped to content hierarchy from headings to captions.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="token-card">
            <div class="token-card-head"><h4>Backgrounds</h4><span class="count">5 layers deep</span></div>
            <p>Primary → Secondary → Tertiary (1 &amp; 2) → Accent. Each layer semantically named so nesting feels automatic, not manual.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="token-card">
            <div class="token-card-head"><h4>Borders &amp; Dividers</h4><span class="count">4 weights</span></div>
            <p>Extra-light, Light, Dark, Extra-dark — separate tokens for dashboard vs. website contexts.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="sub-h">Components in use</h3>
        <p class="sub-p">A snapshot of patterns assembled from the same tokens — date picker, search + checkbox list, label group, list item, avatar stack, progress bar, pagination and card.</p>
        <figure class="system-figure">
          <img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dfim5nugc/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/components-grid_r3lphc" alt="A selection of AjnaLens design system components" />
          <figcaption class="system-figure-caption">
            <span class="lbl">Components</span>
            <span>8 patterns built on the same set of color, spacing and type tokens.</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h3 class="sub-h">The full spec sheet</h3>
        <p class="sub-p">Button states, semantic text and background colors, border weights and the responsive typescale — all defined once and referenced everywhere.</p>
        <figure class="system-figure">
          <img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dfim5nugc/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/system-spec_huowny" alt="Full design system specification" />
          <figcaption class="system-figure-caption">
            <span class="lbl">Foundations</span>
            <span>Button states · semantic text &amp; background colors · border weights · mobile and tablet typescales.</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h3 class="sub-h">Responsive typescale</h3>
        <p class="sub-p">A harmonious scale across four breakpoints — every token named, sized and weighted for its exact purpose in the hierarchy.</p>
        <div class="typescale">
          <div class="typescale-row"><span class="device">Mobile</span><span class="val">h1: 32 / 40</span><span class="meta">body: 14 / 20 · 10 tokens</span></div>
          <div class="typescale-row"><span class="device">Tablet Portrait</span><span class="val">h1: 40 / 48</span><span class="meta">body: 16 / 24 · 10 tokens</span></div>
          <div class="typescale-row"><span class="device">Tablet Landscape</span><span class="val">h1: 40 / 48</span><span class="meta">body: 16 / 24 · 10 tokens</span></div>
          <div class="typescale-row"><span class="device">Desktop Large</span><span class="val">h1: 56 / 64</span><span class="meta">body: 18 / 24 · 10 tokens</span></div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="sub-h">Spacing system</h3>
        <p class="sub-p">16 tokens from 2px to 80px — from icon-text micro-gaps to major section breaks.</p>
        <div class="spacing-grid">
          <div class="spacing-card"><div class="head"><span class="token">Spacing-1</span><span class="px">2px</span></div><div class="bar" style="width:6%"></div><p class="use">Icon-text gaps, badge padding</p></div>
          <div class="spacing-card"><div class="head"><span class="token">Spacing-5</span><span class="px">16px</span></div><div class="bar" style="width:22%"></div><p class="use">Button padding, avatar spacing</p></div>
          <div class="spacing-card"><div class="head"><span class="token">Spacing-9</span><span class="px">32px</span></div><div class="bar" style="width:45%"></div><p class="use">Card internal spacing</p></div>
          <div class="spacing-card"><div class="head"><span class="token">Spacing-16</span><span class="px">80px</span></div><div class="bar" style="width:100%"></div><p class="use">Major section breaks</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 04 Craft -->
      <section class="section reveal">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="num">04</span><span>The craft</span></div>
        <h2 class="section-h">Dark mode wasn't a feature. <span class="accent">It was a proof of architecture.</span></h2>
        <figure class="system-figure">
          <img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dfim5nugc/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/switch-modes_vbxueo" alt="One-click dark mode toggle across all components" />
          <figcaption class="system-figure-caption">
            <span class="lbl">Modes</span>
            <span>One Figma variable mode change — every component switches instantly.</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="craft-pair">
          <div class="craft-card">
            <div class="tag">Variables → Modes</div>
            <p>Figma variable modes meant dark mode wasn't a separate file or a duplication nightmare. One click. Every component. Every screen.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="craft-card">
            <div class="tag">Layered Components</div>
            <p>Clear override logic so designers could customize without breaking the system. Flexibility without chaos.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3 class="sub-h" style="margin-top:32px;">Constraints &amp; trade-offs</h3>
        <ul class="constraints">
          <li>Needed to work with existing design legacy where possible.</li>
          <li>Prioritized depth over breadth — fewer components, better quality.</li>
          <li>Scoped system to 2D only for faster adoption across teams.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 05 Impact -->
      <section class="section reveal">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="num">05</span><span>Impact</span></div>
        <h2 class="section-h">Numbers that <em>moved.</em></h2>
        <div class="impact-grid">
          <div class="impact-card"><div class="v">40%</div><div class="l">Faster design workflow for common flows</div></div>
          <div class="impact-card"><div class="v plain">Fewer</div><div class="l">Dev questions, clearer specs end-to-end</div></div>
          <div class="impact-card"><div class="v">1-click</div><div class="l">Dark mode toggle adopted across all tools</div></div>
          <div class="impact-card"><div class="v plain">All</div><div class="l">Starting point for every new internal product</div></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 06 Reflection -->
      <section class="section reveal">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="num">06</span><span>Reflection</span></div>
        <h2 class="section-h">The biggest win wasn't <span class="accent">the dark mode toggle.</span></h2>
        <div class="takeaway-main">
          <p class="quote">"Working on Ajna taught me the power of good structure. Small decisions in token naming or variable logic can impact teams weeks later."</p>
          <p class="sub">The dark mode toggle was fun to build. But the biggest win was watching other designers move faster, with less friction. That's what a design system is actually for.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reflection-pair">
          <div class="reflection-card">
            <div class="tag">What stuck</div>
            <p>Variables aren't just a Figma feature — they're a way of thinking about decisions that need to scale.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reflection-card">
            <div class="tag">What I'd do differently</div>
            <p>Start with developer feedback earlier. The best tokens are the ones engineers actually want to use.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Footer CTA -->
      <div class="footer-cta reveal">
        <div class="t">Want to <em>play with the system?</em></div>
        <a href="https://www.figma.com/proto/eYEj62rA6f9GXFZiSTiwkI/Babble-Redesign-Challenge?node-id=1417-4672&t=r4u1sYRGGr6ICOfZ-0&scaling=min-zoom&content-scaling=fixed&page-id=58%3A2625&starting-point-node-id=58%3A2745" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary">Open Figma prototype <span class="arr">↗</span></a>
      </div>

      <div class="page-next reveal">
        <a href="/case-smartband" class="prev">
          <span class="k">← Previous</span>
          <span class="v">Smartband for Women</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/case-babbel" class="next">
          <span class="k">Next →</span>
          <span class="v">Babbel · App redesign</span>
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </main>
</CaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  .sub-h {
    font-family: var(--f-display); font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 16px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--fg); margin: 12px 0 8px;
  }
  .sub-p { font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.65; max-width: 60ch; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .built-for {
    margin-top: 28px; font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--fg-dim);
  }

  /* Numbered list */
  .num-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 32px 0 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
  .num-list li { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 18px; font-size: 16px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.6; }
  .num-list .n {
    flex: 0 0 32px; height: 32px; margin-top: 2px;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 50%, transparent);
    font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--accent-ink);
  }

  /* Insight cards */
  .insight-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .insight-card {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 18px; padding: 18px 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-2); border-radius: 12px;
    transition: border-color .3s, background .3s, transform .4s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1);
  }
  .insight-card:hover {
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 50%, var(--line));
    background: var(--bg-3); transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  .insight-card .n {
    flex: 0 0 32px; height: 32px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 50%, transparent);
    font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--accent-ink);
  }
  .insight-card p { font-size: 15px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.55; }

  /* System figure */
  .system-figure { margin: 36px 0 24px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-2); border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden; transition: border-color .3s; }
  .system-figure:hover { border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 50%, var(--line)); }
  .system-figure img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .system-figure-caption { padding: 14px 20px 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.55; }
  .system-figure-caption .lbl { font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent-ink); }

  /* Token grid */
  .token-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin-top: 32px; margin-bottom: 64px; }
  .token-card { border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-2); border-radius: 14px; padding: 28px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; transition: border-color .3s, background .3s, transform .4s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1); }
  .token-card:hover { border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 50%, var(--line)); background: var(--bg-3); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .token-card-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }
  .token-card h4 { font-family: var(--f-display); font-weight: 400; font-size: 17px; letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--fg); }
  .token-card .count { font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent-ink); padding: 4px 10px; border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 30%, transparent); border-radius: 999px; }
  .token-card p { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.65; }

  /* Typescale */
  .typescale { border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-2); border-radius: 14px; padding: 8px 24px; margin: 24px 0 64px; }
  .typescale-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr 1.4fr; gap: 16px; align-items: center; padding: 14px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .typescale-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .typescale-row .device { font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 11px; color: var(--accent-ink); letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .typescale-row .val { font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-muted); }
  .typescale-row .meta { font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 11px; color: var(--fg-dim); text-align: right; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .typescale-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 8px; } .typescale-row .meta { grid-column: 1 / -1; text-align: left; } }

  /* Spacing grid */
  .spacing-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; margin-top: 24px; }
  .spacing-card { border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-2); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .spacing-card .head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .spacing-card .token { font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 11px; color: var(--accent-ink); letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  .spacing-card .px { font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 11px; color: var(--fg-dim); }
  .spacing-card .bar { height: 4px; border-radius: 2px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent), var(--accent-ink)); opacity: 0.5; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .spacing-card .use { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.5; }

  /* Craft pair */
  .craft-pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin-top: 32px; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .craft-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .craft-card { border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-2); border-radius: 14px; padding: 28px; transition: border-color .3s, background .3s, transform .4s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1); }
  .craft-card:hover { border-color: var(--fg-dim); background: var(--bg-3); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .craft-card .tag { font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent-ink); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .craft-card p { font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.65; }

  /* Constraints */
  .constraints { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .constraints li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .constraints li::before { content: ''; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); opacity: 0.6; flex-shrink: 0; }

  /* Impact grid */
  .impact-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .impact-card { text-align: center; padding: 32px 22px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-2); border-radius: 14px; transition: border-color .3s, background .3s, transform .4s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1); }
  .impact-card:hover { border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 50%, var(--line)); background: var(--bg-3); transform: translateY(-3px); }
  .impact-card .v { font-family: var(--f-display); font-weight: 320; font-size: clamp(28px, 3.6vw, 40px); letter-spacing: -0.022em; line-height: 1; color: var(--accent-ink); font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .impact-card .v.plain { color: var(--fg); font-style: normal; }
  .impact-card .l { font-size: 13px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.55; }

  /* Takeaway / reflection */
  .takeaway-main { border-left: 1px solid var(--accent); padding: 26px 32px; background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 6%, var(--bg-2)); border-radius: 0 14px 14px 0; margin-top: 32px; }
  .takeaway-main .quote { font-family: var(--f-display); font-weight: 320; font-style: italic; font-size: clamp(19px, 2.2vw, 26px); line-height: 1.4; letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--fg); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .takeaway-main .sub { font-size: 15px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.65; }

  .reflection-pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin-top: 24px; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .reflection-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .reflection-card { border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-2); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px; }
  .reflection-card .tag { font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent-ink); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .reflection-card p { font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.65; }

  /* Footer CTA + button */
  .footer-cta { margin-top: clamp(72px, 9vw, 112px); padding: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 56px); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; background: var(--bg-2); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 32px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .footer-cta .t { font-family: var(--f-display); font-weight: 320; font-size: clamp(22px, 2.8vw, 30px); letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--fg); max-width: 24ch; }
  .footer-cta .t em { font-style: italic; color: var(--fg-muted); }
  .btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 14px 22px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--fg); font-weight: 500; transition: all .25s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1); }
  .btn:hover { border-color: var(--fg-dim); gap: 14px; }
  .btn-primary { background: var(--fg); color: var(--bg); border-color: var(--fg); }
  .btn-primary:hover { background: var(--accent-ink); border-color: var(--accent-ink); color: var(--bg); }

  /* Page nav */
  .page-next { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin-top: 24px; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .page-next { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .page-next a { padding: 24px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--bg-2); transition: border-color .25s, transform .4s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1), background .25s; display: block; }
  .page-next a:hover { border-color: var(--fg-dim); transform: translateY(-2px); background: var(--bg-3); }
  .page-next .k { font-family: var(--f-sans); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--fg-dim); margin-bottom: 12px; display: block; }
